{
  "id": "ss.enemy.bristle",
  "name": "Bristle",
  "description": "The burrow's fast chaff — a silverfish out of the wall seams, running the nest's trails and stealing off them, the one thing down here that does not belong to the hive. Drawn from the side and mirrored by the game, like the rest of the roster. The silhouette is a comet: a bright tapering body dragging a fan half again its own length, which nothing else in the game is. The three caudal filaments are fused into one plume rather than drawn as three rods — five thin rods off a small oval is an asterisk at the size this is seen at — and the notches keep them legible as three. The fan is four layers plus the hairs across them and three filaments escaping the edge, all rooted at one collar behind the abdomen, so it sweeps a layer at a time and nothing in it can come away from the rest. The body is ten overlapping tergites cut to its own profile over a dark underside, so the seams read as shadow between plates rather than as stripes painted on a dart, with a scatter of the shed scales this animal is named for across the middle. Legs are two-link chains with a knee, in an alternating tripod with the far pair counter-phased; the antennae are three links each and whip with a lag down their length. A wave runs the tergites from head to tail and grows as it travels, so the body carries the scuttle itself instead of riding rigid while only the plume moves. Cool silver against a roster of warm bone and amber so it never competes with the Replete or the Porter's brood, and the palest body on it — this runs on #372d3f earth and the quickest thing on screen must not be the hardest to see. Gameplay radius 7.",
  "tags": ["ss-enemy", "bristle"],
  "size": [52, 28],
  "meta": {"radius": 7},
